{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535305-w20-spiritual-heritage-with-thw-wyrm","id":1535305,"title":"[W20] Spiritual heritage with thw Wyrm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-08T15:03:23-07:00","id":1535305,"title":"[W20] Spiritual heritage with thw Wyrm","content":"Hey folks\u00a1 Recently I started a W20 chronicle with a friend. He is playing as Ola, a theurge garou with Get of Fenris ancestry and she recently passed the First Change. The thing is that she has a Spiritual heritage (5 dots) with the Wyrm and I want to put it in the focus of the chronicle in a near future but I'm looking for ideas. The thing is that Ola has a connection with the triatic Wyrm as well as the corrupt aspect. For me this is pretty interesting but I feel a bit overwhelm, how could you manage a situation like this? How it could look like this connection with the Wyrm in the Umbra? Could the garous detect her as a &quot;wyrm&quot; tainter?<br /> <br /> The campaing takes place in Sweden in the 80's. The last sessions were about her parents. Erika her mother was a Get of Fenris kinfolk (but knows almost nothing about the garou) meanwhile his father, Aon, is human but has something special (probably has a connection with Changelings). Ola is now in the caern of her mother without a idea of what could happen to her in the near future. Meanwhile Erika wants to see her child at any cost and she's now in the way to the caern. The caern is guarded by Voice in the Mist an Uktena Philodox that wants to take care of the cubs until their Rite of Passage, the rest of the caern is in the mountains celebrating an important ritual but they put some spirits guarding the site. <br /> <br /> All help is appreciated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27558-metalbird","name":"Metalbird","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T20:45:22-07:00","id":1535330,"title":"","content":"Ask her what she intended when she added 5 points of Spirit Heritage with the Wyrm on her character sheet. What kind of things was she thinking would happen? What kind of things are fun for her? This is important because I imagine what most STs would do with this would NOT be fun for most players.<br /> <br /> This background means Wyrm spirits want to cooperate with her and do favors for her because they feel some sort of affinity with her. But favors are always repaid. Chiminage is about building relationships with one's spirit allies/families. It's not one sided. If the PC does not end up doing something for these spirits as they do her favors, she'll eventually end up with notoriety and the Wyrm spirits will become angry with her (and in fact, other spirits will also view the character as being untrustworthy because she doesn't keep her word). Furthermore, this background eventually means other Garou will learn of her affinity with these spirits, and they are going to react very negatively towards that. I see nothing but future problems for this character. Does the PC really want that? Or did the player intend for something else?<br /> <br /> Before you work on the details and flavor text of this, I think you and the player need to have a deep talk about what exactly she was hoping to get out of that background. It is entirely possible she doesn't understand the likely negative consequences of such a background. Maybe another background (or even one of Spirit Heritage with the Wyrm, but at only rank 1), Flaw, or other mechanic might be better suited for the kinds of roleplay she was intending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-08T22:08:34-07:00","id":1535332,"title":"","content":"It's also possible for the banes to be particularly fearful of you rather than friendly (about the only way I can see this working for Gaian Garou).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-09T14:42:28-07:00","id":1535375,"title":"","content":"If anything the severity of the problem is understated. At spirit heritage (Bane) five, you look a lot like a Wyrm spirit in the Umbra--three dots is when you start giving off a Wyrmy aura and four is when you start visibly changing. As soon as this character steps sideways, they're in deep shit. In addition to the Garou's reaction, the local Gaian spirits will not like her presence either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}